  "description": "S254 R-S254-2: one synthetic renewals desk of 38 leases in the rehearsal's RentVine transport shape (the rows tests/browser/renewal-novdec-journey-network.mjs serves). Only the group counts come from the November 5 observation; every name, address, date, amount and id is invented. Dates are anchored to anchorBusinessDate and the loader (scripts/lib/one-path-rehearsal/november-5-mix.mjs) shifts them by whole months, so the working month is always the next calendar month on the Central business date. Groups are read from the rows themselves: a status whose primaryLeaseStatusID is 3 is closed, a status with isPendingMoveOutStatus 1 is a move-out notice, isMonthToMonth 1 is month-to-month, and a recordedCycles date earlier than the lease's RentVine end date is a lease renewed in RentVine. The other leases are active fixed-term leases grouped by end month: the working month, the month before it (four leases that ended on its first four days with nothing recorded) and later. recordedCycles, roles and sheet are seed data beside the source rows: a recorded cycle is app state the rehearsal creates through the app's own save while the stand-in serves the recorded date, roles names the five working-month leases of the litmus handoff with the facts later suites seed for them, and sheet is the synthetic operating Sheet (a blank row for the prepared lease, an agreeing row for the covered lease, a row whose rent differs for the replied lease). The starting commit reads only leases and statuses.",
